{"arguments": [
 {"id": "G19", "name": "Cross-resolution status and accountability", "conclusion": "The framework's claims have varying register strength and must be held accountable through declared bridges and adversarial testing.", "speaker": "Framework author",
  "premises": [
   "Theology and lived reality are strong; physics is modest (describes features, not why); the bridge is declared as structural correspondence, not proof.",
   "Mathematics is partially formalized: the necessary ground argument has five proofs, but the ten-law mappings need adversarial testing.",
   "God holds Himself accountable to truth, and science requires falsifiability.",
   "The framework names its own kill conditions in advance, including a force with no matching structure."
  ],
  "strength": {
   "st1": {"v": 2, "quote": "S397 | Register | Status |"},
   "st2": {"v": 2, "quote": "S401 | **Bridge** | Declared. The bridge is structural correspondence, not proof. |"},
   "st3": {"v": 1, "quote": "S402 | **Mathematics** | Partially formalized. The necessary ground argument has five proofs. The ten-law mappings need adversarial testing. |"},
   "st4": {"v": 1, "quote": "S411 | God holds Himself accountable to truth | Science requires falsifiability | The framework names its own kill conditions in advance |"},
   "st5": {"v": 1, "quote": "S227 A determined skeptic could write the exact opposite essay from the same raw physics."},
   "st6": {"v": 2, "quote": "S400 | **Physics** | Modest. Physics describes the features of such a world; it does not say why the world has those features. |"},
   "st7": {"v": 2, "quote": "S410 | ... kill condition: a force with no matching structure |"},
   "st8": {"v": 1, "quote": "S286 But when the same structure appears across registers, we do not dismiss it merely because it crosses a boundary."}
  },
  "prior_art": "Imre Lakatos, Falsification and the Methodology of Scientific Research Programmes, 1970",
  "originality": {
   "or1": {"v": 1, "quote": "S287 We mark the bridge, name its strength, state its limits, and keep testing.", "why": "Lakatos already requires research programmes to declare hard cores, protective belts and falsification conditions, so this is a variant applied to theology rather than a new argument."},
   "or2": {"v": 1, "quote": "S402 | **Mathematics** | Partially formalized. The necessary ground argument has five proofs. The ten-law mappings need adversarial testing. |", "why": "It adds a register-by-register self-audit table (theology strong, physics modest, math partial) that Lakatos does not supply."},
   "or3": {"v": 2, "quote": "S401 | **Bridge** | Declared. The bridge is structural correspondence, not proof. |", "why": "It makes a cross-domain connection between scientific falsifiability norms and theological accountability (God holds Himself to truth), which the prior art does not make."},
   "or4": {"v": 1, "quote": "S397 | Register | Status |", "why": "It supplies a formal status table across five registers, a small structure the prior art lacks, though it is not an equation or model."}
  },
  "weakest_link": "The claim that the bridge is 'declared' rather than proved does not show how a structural-correspondence bridge can be tested, so the accountability criterion never bites.",
  "develop_next": "Specify concrete pass/fail tests for each declared bridge (what observation would count as the correspondence failing), so the accountability claim becomes operational rather than procedural.",
  "case_map": ["K06", "K16"],
  "domain": "philosophy"
 }
]}
